-- THE FIVE PNS LOTS OF 9/24 (canon 0.30.230). Owner, 2026-09-25, verbatim, with a METRC packages grid: All on 9/24/26 /
-- Silo 1 started: 0800 / Silo 2 started: 1030 / Silo 3: 1800 / Silo 4: 1545 / Silo 5: 1200 / Please fix. The grid: 26049 in
-- Silo 5 (tag ...56829, 6551804.32 g), 26050 in Silo 4 (...56830, 6628358.04 g), 26051 in Silo 3 (...56831, 7058606.92 g),
-- 26052 in Silo 1 (...56832, 6749959.72 g), 26053 in Silo 2 (...56833, 5421256 g); the Harvest Details sheet reads the same
-- grams, the silos 5 / 4 / 3 / 1 / 2, plants 1159 / 1357 / 1363 / 656 / 862, strain Bermuda Triangle with the market strains
-- Jokerz Candy (26049, 26050) and Death Star (26051 to 26053). His picks on the question tool: The sheet's, one correction
-- tote each; Re-point the two, add three. THE TWO BOOKS OF RECORD (0.30.203): the sheet is reality; the app follows it.
--
-- What the pre snapshot (db_backups/20260925-090857_pre_lots_49_53, dumped 2026-09-25T13:08:57Z) shows. The five lots were
-- weighed at PNS on 9/24 (740 to 746 totes each) and finished: 26049 5,262,453 g, 26050 5,174,080 g, 26051 5,601,901 g,
-- 26052 5,606,843 g, 26053 5,343,452 g, each 1,143,117 to 1,456,706 g short of the sheet (26053 77,804 g short). This
-- morning at 12:16Z the owner loaded 26049 into Silo 1 with the clock at 08:00 and 26050 into Silo 2 at 10:30 (the
-- silos' times, the wrong lots: by the sheet Silo 1 holds 26052 and Silo 2 holds 26053), then the crew pencilled 26049's
-- Move To to Silo 5 (its package followed) while its load stayed in Silo 1. 26051, 26052 and 26053 have no load and their
-- packages sit at BARN; 26051 to 26053 have no plant count; no package carries its METRC tag; every batch reads the
-- market strain Bermuda Triangle. Silos 3, 4 and 5 hold no open load.
--
-- THE REPAIR. Per lot: one correction tote so the totes sum to the sheet's whole grams (half up), the header and the
-- package to those grams; the plant count where it is missing; the Move To and the package's location to the sheet's
-- silo; the METRC tag on the package and on the batch; the market strain. The two loads of this morning re-pointed
-- (26049 to Silo 5 with its zero at 12:00, 26050 to Silo 4 at 15:45) and three loads written (26052 in Silo 1 at 08:00,
-- 26053 in Silo 2 at 10:30, 26051 in Silo 3 at 18:00), all 9/24 farm time (EDT, UTC-4), the clock zero equal to loaded_at
-- as Load Silo writes it; one open load per silo after. Nothing is voided. The two empty unload sessions opened by
-- visiting Unload Dry Space are untouched.
--
-- Every statement is guarded by the value it expects, so a second run changes nothing; every change lands in
-- record_change_log under the owner's login with this repair's reason and the fixed stamp 2026-09-25T13:30:00.000Z. Run from
-- app/ at the owner's keyboard:
